.github.com/users/RobertMic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertMic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T21:47:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T21:48:12Z","body":">But a observation, you're not saving the dict fields, you need to click the Add Key/Value Pair to indeed save the data\n\nJust ran into this exact same thing except I was using `PackedScene` as a value in a dict. I also did not realize I needed to click the `Add` button to confirm the operation 🤦.\n\nIt was a pretty stupid mistake on my part but I think this would be a good place to improve the UX? That button is not immediately obvious, especially since no other operation I have encountered so far requires a \"confirm\" action and is instead saved when focus is lost.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814100878/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]